Upload a tile pack to /tiles/<z>/<x>/<y>.jpg with the host-side generator.␀Map options␀+/-␀+␀␀␀Zoom␀␀␀␀Shows the zoom slider␀␀␀Zoom in␀Zoom out␀␀␀␀Back to my position␀Contacts on the map␀Follow me␀␀␀Keeps the map on your position␀␀Quick replies␀␀␀î•µ␀î…¤␀Type a message...␀␀␀Quick reply␀ï„¤ %.5f, %.5f␀␀My position (no GPS fix)␀␀␀␀Edit in Settings â†’ Quick replies␀␀ï Stop␀␀␀␀ï‹ Play␀␀␀␀Hold to record a voice message␀␀Couldn't save the voice message␀%s %lu:%02lu␀␀␀␀%lu:%02lu␀␀␀No networks found (2.4 GHz only)␀␀␀␀Conversations␀␀␀î…”␀No conversations yet␀␀␀␀Pick a contact or a private channel, then give it a pad: generate one and export it to the SD card for the other device, or import theirs.␀␀New conversation␀␀␀␀no pad␀␀Tap to add a pad␀␀␀␀%lu.%lu kHz SF%u␀␀␀␀%lu.%lu kHz␀ï”™  ␀␀␀ï€‡  ␀␀␀ï¹  ␀␀␀*  Unfav␀␀␀␀*  Favorite␀ï€Œ  Unblock␀␀␀␀listens and sends␀␀␀listens␀MediaMesh%s%s, %s␀␀␀ï¹  Join␀␀␀ïƒ   Open chat␀␀ï€“  Admin␀␀ï€¡  Ping␀␀␀ïƒ   Message␀␀␀␀ï‰  Telemetry␀␀ï„¤  Show on map␀␀␀␀ï„¤  Hound␀␀ï„¤  Trace SNR␀␀ï‡«  Range test␀ï„¤  Sightline␀␀ïŒ„  Nickname␀␀␀ï„¤  Stop sharing loc␀␀␀ï„¤  Share my loc␀␀␀ï¹  Reset path␀ï‚“  Share contact␀␀Unfavorite it first␀Not in your contacts␀␀␀␀Self  %.4f, %.4f␀␀␀␀Backlight␀␀␀Medium␀␀F11 on the keyboard steps through these too.␀␀␀␀Keyboard backlight␀␀Keyboard layouts␀␀␀␀Tap the language key (EN) on the on-screen keyboard to cycle through the layouts you turn on.␀␀␀Typing␀␀Pick accented letters as you type. Off is plain typing.␀Accent popups␀␀␀Up to three words over the message that finish or fix the one you're typing, or come next; tap one to use it. Your own words and phrases come first.␀␀␀␀Predictive text␀With Predictive text on, Space fixes or finishes a word that isn't one, as on a phone. Backspace straight after puts back what you typed.␀␀␀Space completes the word␀␀␀␀Dictionary: %d words.␀␀␀Dictionary: downloads over Wi-Fi the first time, or copy dictionaries/words-en.pwd to the SD card's predict folder. Until then, your own words are suggested.␀␀␀Custom (manual)␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 runs MediaMesh beside the off-grid channel (800 kHz above it, 250 kHz SF7) and photos and voice go there. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 is Off: everything, photos and voice too, goes out on the off-grid main radio. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀Picking one applies it straight away.␀␀␀Community preset␀␀␀␀TX dBm␀␀AF␀␀SF is the spreading factor, CR the coding rate, AF the airtime factor. A field applies when you leave it.␀␀␀Max duty cycle␀␀Time on air␀radio2 (MediaMesh)␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. Its SX1262 signals a packet through an I/O expander, not straight to the processor, so it can't hop between two frequencies quickly enough. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. It needs an SX1262, LR1110, LR1121 or LR2021 radio. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀A second frequency the radio switches to and from, listening and sending there.␀Photos & voice␀␀Everything␀␀Photos & voice: Open TAK photos and voice clips, text stays on the main mesh. Everything: every message goes out on both. Per contact or channel: their Radio setting.␀␀Sent on radio2␀␀Share with them␀MediaMesh only: photo and voice requests and answers stay on radio2, so nodes without it can't swap them with you. Share: requests go out on both, and a photo or clip asked for on the main mesh is answered there.␀␀␀␀Main-mesh nodes␀250 kHz sends photos and voice about twice as fast; 125 kHz reaches about 40% farther (both SF7). 2.4 GHz moves radio2 off the 900 MHz band at about the 250 kHz preset's speed (406 kHz SF8), with less range; only LR1121 and LR2021 radios can join it. CR 4/5. Everyone on radio2 must use the same.␀␀␀␀Preset␀␀250 kHz sends photos and voice about twice as fast; 125 kHz reaches about 40% farther. Both SF7, CR 4/5. Everyone on radio2 must use the same.␀␀Relay what this radio hears on radio2, on radio2, like a MediaMesh repeater. Main-mesh traffic isn't relayed (that's Client repeat). Needs radio2 On.␀␀␀Repeat MediaMesh␀␀␀␀Find MediaMesh␀␀Listening...␀␀␀␀Found␀␀␀Find MediaMesh listens on each preset for about 10 s while nearby repeaters are asked to answer. MediaMesh repeaters answer on radio2 too, so the preset they're heard on is the one in use here.␀␀␀Everyone sharing radio2 must use the same settings. The radio switches between both frequencies, so heavy radio2 traffic costs some main-mesh reception.␀␀␀␀Listen main / radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 preamble␀Switch time␀Packets main / radio2␀␀␀Warnings␀␀␀␀Temporary radio2␀␀␀␀Use other radio2 settings for a while, for example to meet another group. They end on their own or on a restart; the settings above come back.␀␀15 min␀␀2 hours␀Use these for␀␀␀Running now␀Photos, voice messages and push-to-talk on Public and #public. Everyone on the mesh shares these channels, so this is off by default.␀␀␀Photos and voice on Public␀␀Only switch this on in an emergency.␀␀␀␀Battery and sensor readings, for nodes that ask. Your location has its own setting below.␀␀␀Answer telemetry requests␀␀␀Most mesh spam is a single character, because it is the cheapest message to send. Dropped silently: no chat entry, no notification, no sound.␀␀␀Ignore 1-character messages␀Apps like MeshCore Open TAK send photos, voice and team tracking as text. Messages between apps are dropped, and the rest become a short label such as Photo. A connected phone app still gets everything.␀␀Hide MediaMesh and TAK texts␀␀␀␀Location sharing␀␀␀␀Chosen contacts only␀␀␀␀Anyone who asks␀Sent only when that contact asks, encrypted to them. Nothing is broadcast. Needs "Answer telemetry requests" on. Pick contacts in a contact's menu.␀Share my location when asked␀␀␀␀Off sends them the shifted position your adverts use (GPS > Location privacy).␀␀Exact position to those contacts␀␀␀␀Routing␀1 byte␀␀2 bytes␀3 bytes␀More bytes tell repeaters apart in a big mesh. Repeaters older than MeshCore 1.14 drop 2 and 3 byte packets.␀␀␀␀Multi-byte routing (path hash)␀␀#region␀Region scope (#tag, blank = none)␀␀␀Channel-specific regions can be set in each channel's settings.␀Turn on only if your repeater re-floods just one region. Otherwise it can block logins and direct messages across regions.␀␀Scope direct msgs to region␀Internal (on-board)
External (MMCX)
Auto (legacy, per transmit)␀Only pick External with an antenna fitted to the external socket. After a reboot it starts on the on-board antenna, unless the switch below is on.␀␀LoRa antenna (P4)␀␀␀Starts on the external socket at every boot. Only for an antenna that stays connected.␀␀Always use the external antenna (MMCX)␀␀Reads packets on a background task so a busy screen can't drop them.␀␀␀␀Buffered receive (experimental)␀Resends a message until a repeater echoes it or the recipient ACKs. Turn off to send once only.␀Retry sends until heard␀Signal probe␀␀␀␀Sends a zero-hop advert when no neighbour has been heard for a while, so the signal reading stays fresh. Neighbours only; nothing is repeated.␀␀Minutes, 1 to 1440.␀Auto advert␀Open Advertise app␀␀Send an advert now, or set how often you re-advertise.␀␀Off silences everything below.␀␀A higher-pitched chime, louder on most buzzers.␀Loud alerts␀ï¨␀Volume␀␀Vibration␀␀␀Buzz for new messages, even with Sound off. Respects Do Not Disturb.␀␀␀␀Vibrate␀Pulse␀␀␀Gentle␀␀Long␀␀␀␀Plays once for a message, twice for a DM, three times for an @ mention. Tap one to feel it.␀Pattern␀Voice messages␀␀1200 (default)␀␀1600␀␀␀␀3200␀␀␀␀Codec2 bit rate. Higher is clearer but takes longer to send: 1600 uses a third more airtime than 1200, 3200 nearly three times as much. Every VE3 app plays all three.␀␀Recording quality␀␀␀Fills in the treble Codec2 leaves out, so voices sound less muffled. Made on the radio from the voice itself; turn off to hear clips as decoded.␀␀␀␀Brighter voice␀␀AI voice restorer␀␀␀Download voice model␀␀␀␀Play a sound for␀␀␀␀Messages␀␀␀␀Direct messages␀A mention has its own sound and switch, so it can get through when messages are quiet.␀␀@ mentions␀␀Silences the message sounds between these times every day. Messages still arrive.␀␀␀+30m␀␀␀␀-30m␀␀␀␀From␀␀␀␀Until␀␀␀MediaMesh: %s␀␀␀MAIN␀␀␀␀RADIO2␀␀Live␀␀␀␀Heard main / radio2␀Sent main / radio2␀␀Share of packets heard on radio2␀␀␀␀Preamble main / radio2␀␀Profile switches